<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ===========================================================================================
       Puts an "Allow all" tile in the Orders category, immediately after Allow.

       <b>A def patch rather than a Harmony patch, so it exists everywhere a designator can.</b>
       specialDesignatorClasses is how RimWorld builds a category's tool list, and every architect
       reads the result: vanilla's, this mod's, and any other mod that draws its own. Injecting the
       designator into our panel's grid at draw time would have produced a button that vanished
       whenever this mod's architect was switched off.

       <b>Insert after Designator_Unforbid, not append to the list.</b> Appending would drop it at the
       end, past the plan tools, a long way from the Allow tile it belongs beside. Order in this list
       is the order in the grid, so matching the Unforbid entry and inserting after it puts the pair
       together no matter what a future RimWorld adds to either end.

       PatchOperationInsert defaults to inserting before the matched node; Append is what makes it
       land after.

       Wrapped in a Conditional so a RimWorld that renames or drops Designator_Unforbid leaves the
       game loading normally with one tool missing, rather than failing the patch. success is Always
       for the same reason: that outcome is a gap, not an error worth a red line on startup.
       =========================================================================================== -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/DesignationCategoryDef[defName="Orders"]/specialDesignatorClasses/li[text()="Designator_Unforbid"]</xpath>
    <success>Always</success>
    <match Class="PatchOperationInsert">
      <xpath>Defs/DesignationCategoryDef[defName="Orders"]/specialDesignatorClasses/li[text()="Designator_Unforbid"]</xpath>
      <order>Append</order>
      <value>
        <li>Gideon.UIOverhaul.Features.Architect.Designator_AllowAll</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
